1
00:00:01,051 --> 00:00:03,518
TONIGHT, THE TIME MACHINE WORKS.

2
00:00:03,538 --> 00:00:06,501
YOU GET ONE TRIP. AND YOU KNOW EXACTLY WHERE.

3
00:00:06,521 --> 00:00:09,482
11 YEARS AGO. 9:14 AT NIGHT.

4
00:00:09,502 --> 00:00:10,521
GRANDMA CALLED.

5
00:00:10,541 --> 00:00:12,209
YOU WERE BUSY. YOU LET IT RING.

6
00:00:12,229 --> 00:00:13,791
BY MORNING, SHE WAS GONE.

7
00:00:13,811 --> 00:00:16,678
LATER, HER NEIGHBOR SAID SOMETHING STRANGE.

8
00:00:16,698 --> 00:00:18,563
SOMEONE SAT WITH HER AT THE END.

9
00:00:18,583 --> 00:00:20,384
A YOUNG PERSON, IN A COAT.

10
00:00:20,404 --> 00:00:21,452
NOBODY KNEW WHO.

11
00:00:21,472 --> 00:00:23,232
NOW YOU CAN FIX IT. THERE'S JUST ONE PROBLEM.

12
00:00:23,814 --> 00:00:25,875
TIME TRAVEL IS USELESS.

13
00:00:25,895 --> 00:00:29,390
GIVE ME THREE MINUTES, AND I'LL PROVE IT.

14
00:00:29,658 --> 00:00:31,413
ATTEMPT ONE. TRAIN CANCELLED.

15
00:00:31,433 --> 00:00:33,027
ATTEMPT TWO. YOUR ZIPPER JAMS.

16
00:00:33,047 --> 00:00:35,594
ATTEMPT THREE. THE TAXI DRIVER KNOWS A SHORTCUT.

17
00:00:35,614 --> 00:00:37,291
HE DOES NOT KNOW A SHORTCUT.

18
00:00:37,311 --> 00:00:38,841
SO YOU CALL YOUR YOUNGER SELF.

19
00:00:38,861 --> 00:00:40,139
GO TO HER. RIGHT NOW.

20
00:00:40,003 --> 00:00:41,439
"(WHO IS THIS? IS THIS A PRANK?)"

21
00:00:40,159 --> 00:00:42,638
HE THINKS IT'S A PRANK. HONESTLY? SO WOULD YOU.

22
00:00:42,658 --> 00:00:44,946
214 TRIES.

23
00:00:44,966 --> 00:00:46,140
IT'S NOT BAD LUCK.

24
00:00:46,160 --> 00:00:47,472
IT'S A RULE.

25
00:00:47,724 --> 00:00:51,305
IN THE 1980S, PHYSICIST IGOR NOVIKOV HAD AN IDEA.

26
00:00:51,325 --> 00:00:52,474
THINK OF HISTORY LIKE A

27
00:00:52,494 --> 00:00:54,482
MOVIE THAT'S ALREADY BEEN FILMED.

28
00:00:54,502 --> 00:00:55,530
YOU CAN BE IN IT.

29
00:00:55,550 --> 00:00:56,770
YOU JUST CAN'T EDIT IT.

30
00:00:56,790 --> 00:00:59,841
SCIENTISTS TESTED IT WITH POOL BALLS. ON PAPER.

31
00:00:59,861 --> 00:01:01,975
A BALL ROLLS INTO A TIME TUNNEL,

32
00:01:01,995 --> 00:01:03,413
AND COMES OUT EARLIER.

33
00:01:03,433 --> 00:01:05,758
IT TRIES TO KNOCK ITS YOUNGER SELF AWAY.

34
00:01:05,778 --> 00:01:07,846
THE MATH SAYS NO.

35
00:01:07,866 --> 00:01:09,516
THE ONLY SHOT THAT WORKS,

36
00:01:09,536 --> 00:01:11,274
KNOCKS THE YOUNG BALL IN.

37
00:01:11,294 --> 00:01:12,648
IT CAN'T STOP ITSELF.

38
00:01:12,668 --> 00:01:14,593
IT CAN ONLY BE THE REASON.

39
00:01:14,613 --> 00:01:15,791
YOU STILL CHOOSE.

40
00:01:15,811 --> 00:01:17,073
INSIDE A STORY THAT ALREADY

41
00:01:17,093 --> 00:01:18,415
HAS YOUR NAME IN IT.

42
00:01:18,435 --> 00:01:20,328
IS ANY OF THIS REAL? KIND OF.

43
00:01:20,348 --> 00:01:23,223
ONE COSMONAUT CAME BACK FROM SPACE,

44
00:01:23,243 --> 00:01:26,424
1/50 OF A SECOND IN THE FUTURE.

45
00:01:26,444 --> 00:01:30,650
FORWARD IS EASY. BACKWARD ONLY WORKS ON PAPER.

46
00:01:30,670 --> 00:01:33,465
NOBODY HAS EVER BUILT A TIME MACHINE.

47
00:01:33,485 --> 00:01:36,528
STEPHEN HAWKING ONCE THREW A PARTY FOR TIME TRAVELERS.

48
00:01:36,548 --> 00:01:39,145
HE SENT THE INVITES AFTER THE PARTY.

49
00:01:39,403 --> 00:01:40,332
NOBODY CAME.

50
00:01:40,352 --> 00:01:40,978
OR SOMEBODY DID,

51
00:01:40,998 --> 00:01:44,506
AND LEFT EVERYTHING EXACTLY AS THEY FOUND IT.

52
00:01:44,526 --> 00:01:45,920
REMEMBER THAT.

53
00:01:46,148 --> 00:01:47,344
THERE'S ONE WAY OUT.

54
00:01:47,364 --> 00:01:51,245
PHYSICIST DAVID DEUTSCH SAID THE UNIVERSE MIGHT SPLIT.

55
00:01:51,265 --> 00:01:54,032
CHANGE THE PAST, AND YOU MAKE A NEW TIMELINE.

56
00:01:54,052 --> 00:01:57,394
YOU COULD SAVE A GRANDMA. JUST NOT YOURS.

57
00:01:57,429 --> 00:01:59,304
YOU DON'T WANT A GRANDMA.

58
00:01:59,382 --> 00:02:00,714
YOU WANT HER.

59
00:02:00,734 --> 00:02:02,945
SO YOU STOP TRYING TO FIX IT.

60
00:02:02,965 --> 00:02:07,331
ATTEMPT 215. YOU JUST GO.

61
00:02:07,605 --> 00:02:09,926
HER DOOR ISN'T LOCKED. IT NEVER WAS.

62
00:02:09,946 --> 00:02:13,307
SAME KITCHEN. SAME TEA. SAME SLOW CLOCK.

63
00:02:13,327 --> 00:02:17,410
9:14. ACROSS TOWN, YOUR PHONE STARTS RINGING.

64
00:02:17,430 --> 00:02:19,105
YOUNGER YOU LETS IT RING.

65
00:02:19,125 --> 00:02:20,758
SHE SEES YOU IN THE DOORWAY.

66
00:02:20,778 --> 00:02:22,207
SHE DOESN'T ASK WHO YOU ARE.

67
00:02:22,227 --> 00:02:24,384
SHE JUST SLIDES A CUP OVER.

68
00:02:24,551 --> 00:02:25,978
AND YOU SIT.

69
00:02:26,972 --> 00:02:28,751
YOU CAN'T STOP WHAT'S COMING.

70
00:02:28,771 --> 00:02:31,058
BUT TONIGHT, SHE ISN'T ALONE.

71
00:02:31,078 --> 00:02:33,222
ACROSS THE STREET, THE NEIGHBOR SEES

72
00:02:33,242 --> 00:02:35,335
A YOUNG PERSON IN A BLUE COAT.

73
00:02:35,355 --> 00:02:37,081
YOU DIDN'T CHANGE A THING.

74
00:02:37,101 --> 00:02:39,777
YOU LEFT EVERYTHING EXACTLY AS YOU FOUND IT.

75
00:02:39,797 --> 00:02:42,289
YOU WERE THE PART NOBODY COULD EXPLAIN.

76
00:02:42,647 --> 00:02:45,191
SO YES. TIME TRAVEL IS USELESS...

77
00:02:45,211 --> 00:02:46,807
UNLESS YOU JUST WANT TO BE THERE.

78
00:02:46,827 --> 00:02:49,009
AND RIGHT NOW IS SOMEBODY'S PAST.

79
00:02:49,029 --> 00:02:50,909
SO WHEN YOUR PHONE RINGS TONIGHT...

80
00:02:51,390 --> 00:02:52,625
PICK UP.

